menu "Image Size Check"

config IMAGE_END_ADDR_LIMIT
	hex "Warn when the image end address exceeds this address (0 = no limit)"
	default 0
	help
	  Post-build check on the generated .bin. The application image always
	  starts at ORIGIN of the App Code region (LMA_CORE) in the linker script,
	  so its end address is simply that origin plus the .bin file size. When
	  the image reaches the address set here, the build prints a warning --
	  the build itself still succeeds.

	  Set this to the FIRST address the image must not occupy, i.e. the start
	  of whatever you are protecting, not the last byte the image may use.
	  To keep everything from 0x1009C000 onwards free, enter 0x1009C000: an
	  image ending on 0x1009BFFF is still accepted, one more byte warns.

	  Leave at 0 to disable the warning. A one-line summary of the image size
	  and the remaining space is printed on every build either way.

	  App Code regions per chip, for reference:

	    RF1301          0x10010000 - 0x100F0000   ( 896 KB)
	    RT584H / RT584L 0x10010000 - 0x101F0000   (1920 KB)
	    RT584HA4        0x10010000 - 0x103F0000   (3968 KB)
	    RT581 / RT582   0x00008000 - 0x000F0000   ( 928 KB)
	    RT583           0x00008000 - 0x001F0000   (1952 KB)

	  Example: to be warned once an RF1301 image passes 768 KB, leaving the
	  last 128 KB of the App Code region as margin, set 0x100D0000.

endmenu
